---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Robot Milling"
  category="Project | Robotic Machining"
  year="2024"
  description="IUT Figeac project exploring robotic machining using an industrial robot equipped with a milling spindle, including cutting-condition definition and reconstruction of Bézier surfaces."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    A robotic machining project developed at IUT Figeac, combining an industrial
    robot, a milling spindle, cutting-condition definition and geometric
    reconstruction of complex Bézier surfaces.
  </p>


  <!-- PROJECT SNAPSHOT -->

  <section class="portfolio-hero">

    <div class="portfolio-outcome">

      <span class="portfolio-kicker">
        Outcome
      </span>

      <h2>
        Turning an industrial robot into a machining system.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project explored the use of a conventional industrial robot as a
        machining platform by integrating a milling head and adapting the process
        to the constraints of robotic machining.
      </p>

      <div class="portfolio-metrics">

        <div>
          <strong>6-axis</strong>
          <span>Industrial robot</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>Milling</strong>
          <span>Machining spindle integration</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>Bézier</strong>
          <span>Complex surface reconstruction</span>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>


    <figure class="portfolio-main-visual">

      <img
        src="/images/projects/robot-milling/robot-milling-main.jpg"
        alt="Industrial robot equipped with a milling spindle"
      />

      <figcaption>
        Robotic machining system | Industrial robot equipped with a milling head
      </figcaption>

    </figure>

  </section>


  <!-- 01 | CONTEXT -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Context
      </h2>

      <p>
        The project was developed during my mechanical engineering studies
        at IUT Figeac.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective was to investigate how a conventional industrial robot
        could be adapted for machining operations by integrating a dedicated
        milling spindle and defining suitable cutting conditions.
      </p>

      <p>
        The project also included a geometric reconstruction component focused
        on complex surfaces represented through Bézier geometry.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


